# Gitea Mirror API as used by GiteaApiClient.cs (docs/API.md, issue #472).
# In Visual Studio, open this file and run each request via
# "Send Request"; the responses appear in the test HTTP output window.
@baseUrl = http://10.10.5.5:4321

# Paste the API key from appsettings.json ("Gitea:ApiKey") here.
# Deliberately no real key in this file – it also serves as documentation
# and the repository is public. Never commit a real key.
@api_key = PASTE_KEY_FROM_appsettings_JSON

# Test targets from https://github.com/Dev-DHCIP (UR, Mockup, SRS)
@test_org = Dev-DHCIP
@test_repo = UR
# A regular user account – POST /api/sync/organization deliberately returns 404 for it
@test_user = MajMcCloud

# Set manually: the "id" from the response of the corresponding creation call
@org_id = COPY_FROM_SYNC_ORGANIZATION_RESPONSE
@repo_id = COPY_FROM_SYNC_RESPONSE

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Catalog
# GET /api/github/repositories – all tracked repositories including their ids
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/github/repositories
x-api-key: {{api_key}}
Accept: application/json

### A single repository by id (id from the catalog above)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/repositories/{{repo_id}}
x-api-key: {{api_key}}
Accept: application/json

### Deliberately wrong id -> 404, does not belong to this account
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/repositories/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
x-api-key: {{api_key}}
Accept: application/json

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- Organizations
### POST /api/sync/organization – role has been optional since v3.45.0 and the bot
### no longer sends it. 200 returns organization.id, 409 returns the stored record.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sync/organization
x-api-key: {{api_key}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "org": "{{test_org}}"
}

### Send again -> 409, but it also contains organization.id
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sync/organization
x-api-key: {{api_key}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "org": "{{test_org}}"
}

### Regression case from issue #472: user account instead of organization -> 404 with a JSON error
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sync/organization
x-api-key: {{api_key}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "org": "{{test_user}}"
}

### Unknown role -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sync/organization
x-api-key: {{api_key}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "org": "{{test_org}}",
  "role": "superadmin"
}

### Organization list: /api/github/organizations, NOT /api/organizations
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/github/organizations
x-api-key: {{api_key}}
Accept: application/json

### A single organization by id (without the repository counts)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/organizations/{{org_id}}
x-api-key: {{api_key}}
Accept: application/json

### Path wrongly guessed by the old docs -> JSON 404 that names method and path
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/organizations
x-api-key: {{api_key}}
Accept: application/json

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- Repositories
### POST /api/sync/repository – 200 (created) or 409 (already tracked),
### in both cases with repository.id.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sync/repository
x-api-key: {{api_key}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "owner": "{{test_org}}",
  "repo": "{{test_repo}}"
}

### Refresh an already tracked repository with force -> 409 with the record
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sync/repository
x-api-key: {{api_key}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "owner": "{{test_org}}",
  "repo": "{{test_repo}}",
  "force": true
}

### From a pasted URL: host + path segments, owner/repo remain required
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sync/repository
x-api-key: {{api_key}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "owner": "{{test_org}}",
  "repo": "{{test_repo}}",
  "host": "github.com",
  "path": ["{{test_org}}", "{{test_repo}}", "tree", "main"]
}

### Repository does not exist at the source -> 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sync/repository
x-api-key: {{api_key}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "owner": "{{test_org}}",
  "repo": "does-not-exist-4711"
}

### owner missing -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sync/repository
x-api-key: {{api_key}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "repo": "{{test_repo}}"
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- Mirror jobs
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/job/mirror-repo
x-api-key: {{api_key}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "repositoryIds": ["{{repo_id}}"]
}

### Re-synchronize repositories that are already mirrored
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/job/sync-repo
x-api-key: {{api_key}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "repositoryIds": ["{{repo_id}}"]
}

### The org job needs the id from the creation response, NOT the organization name
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/job/mirror-org
x-api-key: {{api_key}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "organizationIds": ["{{org_id}}"]
}

### Name instead of id -> 404 (this exact case used to break the bot)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/job/mirror-org
x-api-key: {{api_key}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "organizationIds": ["{{test_org}}"]
}

### Empty id list -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/job/mirror-repo
x-api-key: {{api_key}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "repositoryIds": []
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- API usage pitfalls
### POST without "Content-Type: application/json" -> 403
### "Cross-site POST form submissions are forbidden" (without the header the client sends text/plain)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/job/mirror-repo
x-api-key: {{api_key}}
Accept: application/json

{
  "repositoryIds": ["{{repo_id}}"]
}

### Invalid key -> 401 { "success": false, "error": "Unauthorized" }
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/github/repositories
x-api-key: gm_this_key_is_deliberately_wrong
Accept: application/json

### Missing key -> 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/github/repositories
Accept: application/json
